  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45 degrees incidence. Initialize thicknesses from Round 2 best candidate: [45.47, 66.26, 100.01, 115.66, 54.39, 104.87, 69.43, 114.90, 69.98, 102.33, 64.45, 116.99, 56.99, 108.17, 51.15, 83.29, 45.85, 81.30, 51.66, 104.20, 56.85, 92.37, 39.98, 156.38] nm. Apply hard lower bound of 50nm to all layers (clip any thickness below 50nm to 50nm before optimization). Upper bound 200nm. Optimize for high reflectance in 450-650nm and high transmittance in 700-1000nm using gradient-based thickness optimization. Evaluate unpolarized light. Maximum 24 layers fixed. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a fixed 24-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica at 45° unpolarized incidence to maximize reflectance in 450-650 nm and transmittance in 700-1000 nm while suppressing leakage in reverse bands, subject to 50-200 nm thickness constraints and provided initialization.",
